mumps provides CMake targets:

    find_package(MUMPS CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE MUMPS::DMUMPS)

MUMPS is written in Fortran. Enable Fortran in your project so that CMake links
the Fortran runtime, even if your own sources are C or C++:

    project(my_project LANGUAGES C Fortran)

This port builds MUMPS in sequential mode; it uses the bundled MPI stub, whose
headers are installed to the "mumps_seq" include subdirectory.
